#X obj 682 11 seq.life;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 301 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 A sequencer based on Conway's Game of Life. The object
maintains a two-dimensional grid of cells \, and each call to the next
method advances the grid by one generation \, applying the classic
Game of Life rules: a live cell survives if it has 2 or 3 live neighbors
\, and a dead cell becomes alive if it has exactly 3 live neighbors.
The current state of the grid can be read as a flat list of 0s and
1s.;
#X text 240 214 Typical use cases:;
#X text 250 239 • Generative rhythmic patterns — turning the live cells
of the grid into trigger events \, so that the rhythm evolves organically
over time as the pattern changes.;
#X text 250 294 • Visual and sonic installations — displaying the grid
in real time (for example \, via [ui.matrix]) while mapping cell activity
to sound \, creating a combined audiovisual process.;
